# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "A construct reads the same wherever it legitimately stands"

# Depth is where this grammar has broken: an unclosed run inside a widget, a fence
# inside a tid body, a cell that read nothing at all. Each container below holds a
# construct that must read exactly as it reads at top level.

<<<

|a |[[Some Target]] |
#     ^^^^^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 markup.quote.quoteblock.tiddlywiki5 markup.other.table.tiddlywiki5 markup.link.tiddlywiki5 markup.underline.link.tiddlywiki5

<<<

* an item with ''strong'' in it
#                ^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 markup.list.unnumbered.unordered.ul.li.tiddlywiki5 markup.bold.tiddlywiki5

! a heading with {{Some/Tiddler}}
#                ^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.heading.heading-1.tiddlywiki5 meta.transclusion.transcludeinline.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.transclusion.transcludeinline.begin.tiddlywiki5

|a |<<myMacro one>> |
#     ^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 markup.other.table.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.macrocallinline.tiddlywiki5 variable.name.macro.tiddlywiki5
